{
  "families": [
    {
      "family": "pipelined",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 14, "high": 22, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 8, "high": 20, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": -2, "high": 4, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 4, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]}
      ],
      "budget_share": 0.6,
      "why": "Pipelined gives 1 result/cycle and is the simplest way to meet the 32 requests/us burst: a 32-request burst completes in 32 cycles after a latency of N+2 cycles. The system p99 batch constraint then requires Fmax >= 2*(N+33) MHz, which is plausible for N up to ~20. Data_width is restricted to >=14 because the output LSB is 2^-(W-2) and max_abs_err <= 2^-12 forces W >= 14. n_iter 8..20 trades area against accuracy; angle_guard and frac_guard tune the error/area trade-off. This family is likely the main feasible front, so it gets the larger share."
    },
    {
      "family": "pipelined_m",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 14, "high": 22, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 8, "high": 20, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": -2, "high": 4, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 4, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]},
        {"param": "m", "low": 2, "high": 8, "choices": null}
      ],
      "budget_share": 0.4,
      "why": "Pipelined_m registers every m micro-rotations, reducing pipeline FFs and latency cycles to ceil(N/m)+2. This can lower area, but longer combinational paths may reduce Fmax, which matters for the 0.5 us p99 batch bound. Searching m=2..8 explores the area/latency/Fmax trade-off. Same accuracy-driven bounds on data_width (>=14) and n_iter (8..20) apply. This family may provide cheaper points on the Pareto front if the Fmax penalty is acceptable."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The spec needs 12-bit accuracy (max_abs_err <= 2^-12) and a 32-request burst every 1 us with p99 batch <= 0.5 us. Pipelined families produce 1 result/cycle, so throughput_msps >= 32 is easily met if Fmax >= 32 MHz. The batch constraint is the tighter system limit: for pipelined, batch time is (N+2+31)/Fmax <= 0.5 us, so Fmax must be at least ~2*(N+33) MHz; for pipelined_m it is (ceil(N/m)+2+31)/Fmax <= 0.5 us. Data_width must be >=14 because the output LSB is 2^-(W-2) and W=13 would already exceed the error bound. We therefore search data_width 14..22, n_iter 8..20, angle_guard -2..4, frac_guard 0..4, and both rounding modes. The 60/40 split favours the simpler pipelined family, which is most likely to satisfy the system bound, while pipelined_m explores area savings from fewer pipeline registers. The first round is deliberately broad; later rounds can narrow around the feasible Pareto front and the system-feasible region."
}
